Maintainer: Iain Smith <iain@issinoho.com>
# loadbearer's MSRV is 1.88 and it uses edition 2024, so the distribution's
# default rustc is too old on every current series (noble ships 1.75). The
# versioned toolchains are listed newest-first: apt takes the first
# alternative it can install, which is 1.91 on noble-updates and 1.88 on
# questing. The unversioned fallback is for builders that have a new enough
# default, such as a CI runner using rustup.
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cargo-1.91 | cargo-1.89 | cargo-1.88 | cargo (>= 1.88),
               rustc-1.91 | rustc-1.89 | rustc-1.88 | rustc (>= 1.88)
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Homepage: https://github.com/issinoho/loadbearer
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/issinoho/loadbearer.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/issinoho/loadbearer
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: loadbearer
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: CLI system-assessment and benchmarking tool
 loadbearer benchmarks a machine's CPU, memory, disk and network, scores each
 metric against an embedded reference baseline, and grades every component and
 the machine as a whole on an S-F scale.
 .
 Results save as JSON and can be re-graded against a different baseline without
 re-running the benchmarks, or compared between two machines. A terminal UI
 shows progress while a run is in flight and the results when it finishes.
 .
 Network and sustained-load results are measured and shown but never folded
 into a grade, since they reflect the operating system and cooling rather than
 the silicon.
